; The whole compiler, end to end, on a bundle with a #prelude line.
;
; Unlike the other stage tests this one supplies no main of its own and takes
; the compiler's, because what is under test is the input header of spec
; section 9.1, and parse_bundle is only reachable through it.
;
; The input defines h twice, once on each side of the boundary. The golden
; output is the whole module, so it pins down three things at once: that the
; header was understood, that two functions of the same name can coexist, and
; that they get the l0_p_ and l0_f_ symbols of spec section 10.2, with main
; calling the program's.
